    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d659">

                <pb facs="0997" n="901" sameAs="frus:frus1931-41v01/pg901"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.115/1068</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Oral Statement by the American Ambassador in
                        Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Japanese Minister for
                        Foreign Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Matsuoka</hi>)<anchor n="83" xml:id="d659-f1"/></head>
                <p>The statement marked “oral” which was handed to the American Ambassador on
                    December 17, 1940, by His Excellency the Minister for Foreign Affairs, was
                    referred to the American Government.</p>
                <p>The American Government has now informed the Ambassador that it regrets that this
                    statement cannot be considered as responsive to the representations made by the
                    United States Government to the Government of Japan.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">[<placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi>
                        </placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian" when="1941-01-07">January 7,
                            1941</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d659-f1" n="83" type="source" xml:id="d659-f1-content">
                <p>Handed, on January 7, 1941, to the acting chief of the American Bureau of the
                    Japanese Foreign Office by the first secretary of the American Embassy in Japan
                    (Crocker).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
